   "detail": "34 rows sum to EXACTLY 27,236.46 = the printed TOTAL at the foot of Form B = the cover line-3 CUMULATIVE cell. Cover line 3's LAST REPORT and THIS REPORT cells are both blank, so cumulative is the only printed anchor. The ledger is corroborated as cycle-to-date by its own dates: it opens 1/26/2018, well before the certified period beginning 3/9/2018. NOTE the two sides are on DIFFERENT scopes on this one filing - Form A is per-period, Form B is cumulative - which is exactly why the scope test is run per page."
