 "escalation_note": "p2 and p4 each re-rendered as two 600 dpi amount-column strips for an independent second read of all 74 amounts (every one read identically); p3 table at 500 dpi; six 600 dpi geometry-proof cell crops.",
 "notes": "Generation-2 county-branded form ('WASHINGTON COUNTY CANDIDATE FINANCIAL CAMPAIGN REPORT ... Washington County Code 1-7-1'), typed throughout. ** THE DOCUMENT CONTRADICTS THE CHUNK FILE ON OFFICE: the chunk file / index.csv says 'Commission Seat A', but the cover's 'Office' line is BLANK, as are 'Representative District' and 'In the ___ School District'. The form therefore states no office at all. ** It is not out of scope - it is a Washington County candidate form filed with the Washington County Clerk - but the office attribution comes from outside the document and a human should be aware of that. Candidate name on the form 'Gilbert M. Almquist' agrees with the index. Certified period 3/9/2018 to 6/19/2018; signed 6/19/2018; RECEIVED stamp JUN 19 2018. Candidate street address, ZIP, home phone and business phone are printed in the clear on the cover and were discarded at read time; every donor street address / PO box / ZIP on p2 and p3 was likewise discarded and only city+state retained. p3 is a filer-typed continuation sheet ('ITEMIZED CONTRIBUTION REPORT CONTINUED') in a different typeface from the county form - it is part of the contribution side, not a second report. Two in-kind items appear on BOTH schedules (Judy Bozeman 575.00, Ceri Steele 465.34, and Clark Kelsey 500.00 as 'Clark Kelsey Video'), which is how in-kind is meant to be booked and is not a duplication defect. No page in this PDF is rotated relative to the others; poppler renders all four upright.",
